%  Conventions
%  -----------
%  * Keys are JabRef style: Surname + Year, disambiguated with a/b/c.
%    Let JabRef generate them ("Cleanup entries" -> "Generate BibTeX key").
%  * Entries are grouped by role in the course, in the order the course uses
%    them. Add new entries to the group they belong to, not at the end.
%  * Abstracts, file paths, keyword lists and urldate fields are deliberately
%    stripped: this file is read by humans and by two different citation
%    processors, and those fields break both.
%  * A one-line comment above an entry says what the course uses it FOR.
%    Keep that habit -- it is what makes a 200-entry file navigable.
%
%  See bibliography-keymap.md for the mapping from the three pre-merge files.
